%N A400941 The number of order-preserving or reversing partial permutations of an n-element set.
%H A400941 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400941/b400941.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A400941 V. H. Fernandes, G. M. S. Gomes and M. M. Jesus, <a href="https://zbmath.org/1208.20057">The cardinal and the idempotent number of various monoids of transformations on a finite chain</a>, Bull. Malays. Math. Sci. Soc. (2), 34(1) (2011), 79-85. See Theorem 2.1.
%F A400941 a(n) = 2*binomial(2*n, n) - n^2 - 1.
%F A400941 From _Stefano Spezia_, Oct 10 2026: (Start)
%F A400941 G.f.: 2/sqrt(1 - 4*x) - (1 - x + 2*x^2)/(1 - x)^3.
%F A400941 E.g.f.: 2*exp(2*x)*BesselI(0, 2*x) - exp(x)*(1 + x + x^2).
%F A400941 a(n) ~ 2^(2*n+1)/sqrt(n*Pi). (End)
%t A400941 A400941[n_] := 2*Binomial[2*n, n] - n^2 - 1; Array[A400941, 30, 0] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 16 2026 *)
